`SpringBrowserlessTest` itself carries:
```java
@ExtendWith(SpringExtension.class)
@TestExecutionListeners(listeners = BrowserlessTestSpringLookupInitializer.class,
                         mergeMode = MergeMode.MERGE_WITH_DEFAULTS)
```
It has an `@Autowired ApplicationContext applicationContext` field, a `@BeforeEach initVaadinEnvironment(...)`, and `@AfterEach cleanVaadinEnvironment()`. Your test class must still add `@SpringBootTest` (with your `@SpringBootApplication`/config class) since `SpringBrowserlessTest` only wires `SpringExtension` — it relies on the enclosing Spring test context being bootstrapped normally.

**Key methods (from `BaseBrowserlessTest`):**
```java
<T extends Component> T navigate(Class<T> viewClass);
<T extends Component> T navigate(String url, Class<T> viewClass);
<T extends ComponentTester<Y>, Y extends Component> T test(Y component);   // dispatches via TesterWrappers overloads
<T extends Component> ComponentQuery<T> $(Class<T> componentClass);         // = find(...), searches whole UI
<T extends Component> ComponentQuery<T> $view(Class<T> componentClass);     // scoped to current view
```
`ComponentQuery<T>` is a fluent locator: `.withLabel(...)`, `.withCaption(...)`, `.withText(...)`, `.withId(...)` etc., terminated by `.single()`/`.first()`/`.all()`/`.exists()`.

